.TH CCOL_ITER_KEY_PTR 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
ccol_iter_key_ptr \- get a typed const pointer to the current key
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <citerators.h>   /* or any container header */

const KeyT *ccol_iter_key_ptr(it);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Returns a typed const pointer to the key of the element currently
pointed to by it.

For cvec iterators the key is the element index (size_t).
For chmap and cbmap iterators the key is the actual map key.
Char-pointer keys are returned as (const char **) pointing into the
map's internal storage; all other key types are returned as a direct
typed pointer.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
it   Iterator variable declared with ccol_iter_declare() or inside
     ccol_for_each().
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
const KeyT* to the current key.  Do not free or mutate the pointed-to
value through this pointer.
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
The returned pointer is valid only while the iterator is alive and
the container has not been modified.
Uses a GNU C statement expression; requires GCC or Clang.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ccol_iter_val_ptr (3),
.BR ccol_iter_declare (3)
